  "introduction": {
    "text": "The Basilica di Santa Cecilia in Trastevere is a titular church and minor basilica in Rome dedicated to Saint Cecilia, patron saint of music. It has served as a cardinal titular church since the 5th century and is renowned for its rich history, architectural features, and artistic treasures, including mosaics, frescoes, and relics that attract pilgrims and musicians worldwide.",
    "sourceIds": ["wikipedia"]
  },
